cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FigureLab: a browser-based tool for assembling publication-quality scientific figures"
message: "If you use FigureLab in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Baffour Awuah"
    given-names: "Michael"
    affiliation: "Ramsey Lab, Department of Biology, Texas A&M University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-9036-413X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mbaffour/FigureLab"
url: "https://mbaffour.github.io/FigureLab/"
abstract: >-
  FigureLab is a single-file, browser-based application for assembling
  publication-quality scientific figures from image data (microscopy, western
  blots, histology, gels, and clinical or specimen photographs). It runs
  entirely client-side with no installation, server, or internet connection
  required, so no image data ever leaves the user's computer. Features include
  grid layout with drag-to-space gutters, per-panel image adjustments
  (brightness, contrast, gamma, levels, fluorescence LUTs, and multi-channel
  composites), two-point scale-bar calibration, an annotation system with
  undo/redo, and export to PNG, JPEG, WebP, TIFF, PDF, and SVG at
  publication DPI (up to 1200 dpi for line art). It also exports reproducibility
  scripts (R/Python), CSV panel metadata, and journal-style captions.
keywords:
  - "scientific figures"
  - "microscopy"
  - "image analysis"
  - "publication"
  - "reproducibility"
  - "western blot"
  - "scale bar"
  - "open science"
  - "bioimaging"
license: MIT
version: "3.5"
date-released: "2026-07-08"
